只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A local-first workspace for human-led collaboration with multiple AI employees.","id":"gh:1245185760","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"orbit","slug":"kevinforge/orbit","topics":["agentic-workflow","ai-agents","ai-coding","claude-code","codebuddy","codex","coding-agents","dsh","dsh-plugin","multi-agent"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A local-first workspace for human-led collaboration with multiple AI employees."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Orbit"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"中文 · English"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A local-first workspace for human-led collaboration with multiple AI employees."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Coordinate Claude Code, Codex, and CodeBuddy in one conversation, one workspace at a time."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What Orbit is"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Orbit turns a local project directory into a collaborative AI workbench. You\ndefine a team of digita"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"l employees, give each employee a role and an execution\nruntime, and coordinate their work through a"},{"id":"p7s3","text":" shared conversation. Orbit keeps\nthe user in control while the employees clarify requirements, desi"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"gn a plan,\nimplement changes, verify results, and hand work to one another."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The employees are powered by Claude Code, Codex, or CodeBuddy through the Agent\nClient Protocol (ACP"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"). Orbit owns the workspace, conversation history, routing,\nqueues, approvals, session continuity, a"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"nd UI; each vendor runtime remains\nresponsible for its own model access and tool execution."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## 📦 Installation"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"If you already use Claude Code, Codex, or CodeBuddy locally, copy this prompt\nto your agent:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## See it in action"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Orbit can turn one unassigned goal into a supervised multi-agent workflow:\nthe supervisor decomposes"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" the work, specialists investigate in parallel, a\nverification employee checks the deliverables, and"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" the supervisor produces the\nfinal synthesis in the same conversation."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"This demo was recorded from a real ACP/model run with Claude Code, Codex, and\nCodeBuddy in the `复杂协作"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"` mode. The demonstration project is isolated from\nthe Orbit source tree and contains no private wor"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ration project is isolated from\nthe Orbit source tree and contains no private workspace information."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Why use it"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **One conversation, several specialists.** Keep requirements, design,\nimplementation, and verifica"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"tion in the same visible work stream.\n- **Human-directed routing.** Assign work explicitly with the "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"employee's\ndisplay name, or let supervised mode coordinate an unassigned goal.\n- **Runtime choice pe"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"r employee.** Mix Claude Code, Codex, and CodeBuddy in one\nteam and change the assignment later from"},{"id":"p16s5","text":" the UI.\n- **Local-first state.** Workspaces, messages, configuration, runtime sessions,\nattachments"},{"id":"p16s6","text":", and transcripts are stored under `~/.orbit`.\n- **Recoverable execution.** Runs are queued per empl"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"oyee, streamed to the UI,\ncancellable, approval-aware, and isolated by workspace and conversation."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"All three runtimes use ACP v1 over newline-delimited JSON-RPC on stdio. Orbit\nmaps their streamed up"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"dates into a common activity model, while runtime-specific\nbehavior stays inside the corresponding a"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"nto a common activity model, while runtime-specific\nbehavior stays inside the corresponding adapter."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Core concepts"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Concept | Meaning |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Workspace | A local project directory with its own employee configuration and collaboration data. "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"|\n| Conversation | A durable channel inside a workspace. Multiple conversations can run independentl"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"y. |\n| Digital employee | A user-configurable role with a display name, prompt, enabled state, and s"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"elected runtime. |\n| Assignment | Work addressed with `@display-name:`. The display name is the publ"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"ic routing key; internal IDs are not. |\n| Runtime session | The vendor-side ACP session restored for"},{"id":"p22s6","text":" an employee when the next run starts. |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Three interaction modes"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Every conversation has a mode. The mode affects how messages are routed; it\ndoes not erase an employ"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ee's persisted runtime session."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Mode | Best for | Routing behavior |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| **普通对话** (direct) | A focused conversation with one employee | Assign one employee with `@display-"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"name:`. Later unmarked messages continue with that employee. |\n| **简单协作** (collaborative) | Explicit"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" multi-person teamwork | Assign one or more employees. Employees can hand work to one another when n"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"eeded. |\n| **复杂协作** (supervised) | A goal that needs decomposition and follow-up | Send an unassigne"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"d goal to the internal supervisor, which schedules the configured employees. |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Requirements"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- At least one installed and authenticated runtime: Claude Code, Codex, or\nCo"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"deBuddy with ACP support.\n- Bun is also required when building the standalone executable from source"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"eBuddy with ACP support.\n- Bun is also required when building the standalone executable from source."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Orbit includes the ACP protocol adapters for Claude Code and Codex. You do not\nneed to install `clau"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"de-agent-acp` or `codex-acp` separately. CodeBuddy is\ninstalled separately, for example with `npm in"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"stall -g @tencent-ai/codebuddy-code`,\nand must be able to run its ACP mode on the local machine."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"- Three interaction modes for direct work, explicit collaboration, and\nsupervised collaboration.\n- C"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"onfigurable digital employees and reusable workspace team templates.\n- Claude Code ACP, Codex ACP, a"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"nd CodeBuddy ACP runtime adapters.\n- Per-message approval modes: ask before tool operations or appro"},{"id":"p32s4","text":"ve the current\ntask automatically.\n- Human-in-the-loop permission requests and structured elicitatio"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"n forms or\nexternal URLs.\n- Per-employee FIFO run queues, cancellation, interruption, and failure st"},{"id":"p32s6","text":"ate.\n- Multiple conversations with background execution and live activity updates.\n- Durable message"},{"id":"p32s7","text":" history, runtime session restoration, attachments, and\nterminal transcripts.\n- Collaboration Insigh"},{"id":"p32s8","text":"ts for task outcomes, execution timelines, and duration\ntrends.\n- A local HTTP server, React UI, SSE"},{"id":"p32s9","text":" event stream, and standalone binaries for\nsupported platforms."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Data and privacy"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Orbit's own product data is stored locally under `~/.orbit`; it is not stored in\nthis repository. Ru"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ntime authentication and model-provider behavior are owned by\nthe vendor CLI you choose, so network "},{"id":"p34s3","text":"access and account policies depend on\nthat runtime."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Read Local Data before backing up, moving, retaining,\nor resetting Orbit data. Read Terminology And "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"Routing\nbefore building integrations around employee names or assignment markers."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Support and security"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Use GitHub Issues for reproducible\nbugs and feature requests. For security issues, follow SECURITY.m"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"d\ninstead of posting sensitive details publicly. General support expectations are\ndescribed in SUPPO"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"ead of posting sensitive details publicly. General support expectations are\ndescribed in SUPPORT.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
